    passageEn: "Earth's outermost lithosphere is fragmented into vast tectonic plates that float continuously atop the semi-molten asthenosphere. At fault boundaries, immense frictional resistance locks adjacent rock masses together while convection currents continuously apply relentless pressure. When accumulated elastic strain eventually overcomes friction, the crust ruptures violently, unleashing seismic energy waves in all directions. These profound geological events deform mountain ranges, trigger tsunamis, and reshape regional continental coastlines over epochs. Analyzing seismic vibrations with sensitive seismographs enables geologists to unravel the mysterious inner structure of Earth's planetary core.",
